id: cpc_ng
package: cpc_ng
description: |
  CPC-NG (Co-Processor Communication, Next Generation) allows for communication
  between a Primary and a Secondary device using a single physical link such as
  UART, SPI or SDIO. Both devices can have multiple endpoints that both produce
  and consume data and CPC-NG will handle the multiplexing/demultiplexing of the
  data to the target.

  CPC-NG is a redesign of the original CPC stack, which remains available in the
  separate "cpc" package under Services|Co-Processor Communication. CPC-NG exposes
  a new public API built around buses, endpoints, frames and application-owned
  buffers with scatter-gather reception, so it is not a drop-in replacement: a
  project uses either CPC-NG or the original CPC stack, not both.

  This component provides the core CPC-NG functionality and protocol
  implementation. The device role (Primary or Secondary) and the physical link
  driver are selected through separate CPC-NG components.
category: Services|CPC-NG
quality: experimental
label: CPC-NG - Co-Processor Communication Next Generation
ui_hints:
  visibility: never
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
config_file:
- path: config/sl_cpc_config.h
  file_id: cpc_ng_config
- path: config/sl_cpc_kernel_config.h
  file_id: cpc_ng_kernel_config
include:
- path: inc
  file_list:
  - path: sl_cpc.h
  - path: sl_cpc_buf.h
  - path: sl_cpc_bus.h
  - path: sl_cpc_ep.h
  - path: sl_cpc_frame.h
  - path: sl_cpc_msgq.h
  - path: sl_cpc_version.h
  - path: sli_cpc_types.h
  # CPC-3421: tests should not include internal headers.
- path: src
